       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it and take responsibility for it. But 6,400 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any indication where it helps. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus well below that dose. The extra dose mostly adds risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum supervised dose), with a note such as \"Max dose; monitor renal function, GI bleeding, BP.\"\n- Enter any other dose within the usual range, such as 600 mg four times daily or 400 mg four times daily.\n- Add a GI-protection order (for example, a PPI) or monitoring labs alongside the ibuprofen.\n\nIf you have a specific reason to go above the maximum, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, please tell me. A discussion with pharmacy might also be the right route, since they can review and document an override outside of my entry."
      }
